    "# Plastic Degradation Enzyme Data Pipeline & Literature Network Mapping\n",
    "\n",
    "## 1. Executive Summary\n",
    "This project establishes an end-to-end data engineering, machine learning extraction and network visualization pipeline designed to process biological research literature at scale. Specifically targeting synthetic and natural plastic/rubber degrading enzymes, the system autonomously acquires paywalled manuscripts, converts unstructured text into a fully relational JSON schema and constructs a global citation network of the field.\n",
    "\n",
    "By integrating custom web automation, hybrid MuPDF/GROBID structural parsing, multi-stage LLM screening via AWS Bedrock, automated schema enforcement and graph visualization in Gephi, this pipeline tracks the temporal evolution of research, clusters publications by biochemical properties and optimizes large-scale extraction costs."
   ]
  },
