   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 2. Corpus Genesis & Iterative Citation Expansion\n",
    "The foundation of the dataset was built using a highly targeted multi-generational search strategy. The process began with building a concentrated seed database and iteratively expanding it through citation networks.\n",
    "\n",
    "### Phase 1: Seed Generation & Initial Triage\n",
    "* **Source Compilation:** Initial literature was aggregated from three primary streams. The PAZy database API provided DOIs, PETadex NR accessions yielded roughly 6,000 papers and a custom broad keyword scraping script gathered the remainder. This combined ingestion created a foundational corpus of approximately 11,600 papers.\n",
    "* **Acquisition & Conversion:** Full texts for these initial sources were autonomously scraped as PDFs and converted into structured JSONs using the hybrid MuPDF and GROBID pipeline.\n",
    "* **Keyword & LLM Filtering:** The raw JSON text was passed through a keyword filter to isolate documents discussing potential plastic-degrading enzymes, reducing the pool from 11,600 to roughly 10,000 papers. A subsequent stringent screening pass using an LLM identified manuscripts containing concrete enzymatic activity data, resulting in a highly curated core of 900 seed papers.\n",
    "\n",
    "### Phase 2: Iterative Bidirectional Citation Expansion\n",
    "* To map the broader landscape, the project utilized Litmaps to perform bidirectional citation traversal based on the 900 seed papers.\n",
    "* **First-Order Expansion:** For each seed paper, the top 200 forward citations and top 200 backward references were queried. This expanded the network to roughly 40,000 papers. Abstract and title screening via RIS exports filtered this massive pool down to 3,400 highly relevant candidates.\n",
    "* **Second-Order Expansion:** The bidirectional expansion was repeated on those 3,400 candidates, generating a macro-network of 100,000 papers. A final rigorous screening pass distilled this network down to a concentrated corpus of 4,600 highly relevant papers.\n",
    "* **Final Ingestion:** The final 4,600 papers undergo full-text scraping, JSON conversion and ingestion into the deep extraction pipeline."
   ]
