    "## 3. Automated Corpus Acquisition & Network Crawling\n",
    "To support the iterative expansion and acquire full texts for the entire corpus, the pipeline relies on a custom-built automation engine capable of both targeted DOI fetching and broad keyword pagination.\n",
    "* **Institutional Proxy Integration:** The scraper authenticates via the university library proxy (EZProxy) to bypass publisher paywalls and access full-text PDFs.\n",
    "* **Keyword Search & Pagination:** The engine can execute broad queries (e.g. \"plastic degradation enzymes\") and autonomously paginate through hundreds of library search results. It features dynamic waits and UI state verification to ensure it never desynchronizes during long scraping runs.\n",
    "* **Dynamic Bot Evasion & Navigation:** Utilizes `undetected_chromedriver` combined with PyAutoGUI fallback mechanisms to navigate complex publisher portals. It successfully handles EPUB/viewer frames and circumvents bot-verification checks.\n",
    "* **Stateful File Tracking:** The system monitors local directory states to confirm successful background downloads. It instantly renames incoming files to sanitized identifiers to ensure seamless downstream processing.\n",
    "* **System Resiliency:** Built for high-volume execution, the engine features automated resume logic, comprehensive error logging to CSV files, rate-limit pacing and dynamic memory-crash recovery to revive the browser during out-of-memory failures."
